text: ['({T}: Add {B} or {R}.)', '({T}: Add {B}.)', '({T}: Add {G} or {W}.)', '({T}: Add {G}.)', '({T}: Add {R} or {G}.)', '({T}: Add {R}.)', '({T}: Add {U} or {B}.)', '({T}: Add {U}.)', '({T}: Add {W} or {U}.)', '({T}: Add {W}.)', 'Add {B} for each creature card in your graveyard.', 'All creatures lose flying until end of turn.\\nSacrifice a snow land: Return Whiteout from your graveyard to your hand.', "As An-Zerrin Ruins enters the battlefield, choose a creature type.\\nCreatures of the chosen type don't untap during their controllers' untap steps.", "As Lost Order of Jarkeld enters the battlefield, choose an opponent.\\nLost Order of Jarkeld's power and toughness are each equal to 1 plus the number of creatures the chosen player controls.", 'As an additional cost to cast this spell, exile a creature you control.\\nReturn target creature card from your graveyard to the battlefield. Put a +2/+2 counter on that creature if the exiled creature was a Thrull.', 'As an additional cost to cast this spell, pay 3 life.\\nDestroy target creature and target land.', 'As an additional cost to cast this spell, sacrifice a creature.\\nGain control of target nonartifact, nonblack creature.', 'As long as Juniper Order Advocate is untapped, green creatures you control get +1/+1.', 'At end of combat, if Kjeldoran Home Guard attacked or blocked this combat, put a -0/-1 counter on Kjeldoran Home Guard and create a 0/1 white Deserter creature token.', 'At the beginning of each end step, if a creature dealt damage by Krovikan Vampire this turn died, put that card onto the battlefield under your control. Sacrifice it when you lose control of Krovikan Vampire.', 'At the beginning of the end step, if Krovikan Horror is in your graveyard with a creature card directly above it, you may return Krovikan Horror to your hand.\\n{1}, Sacrifice a creature: Krovikan Horror deals 1 damage to any target.', 'At the beginning of the end step, if no creatures are on the battlefield, sacrifice Withering Wisps.\\n{B}: Withering Wisps deals 1 damage to each creature and each player. Activate no more times each turn than the number of snow Swamps you control.', 'At the beginning of your upkeep, flip a coin. If you lose the flip, Mana Crypt deals 3 damage to you.\\n{T}: Add {C}{C}.', 'At the beginning of your upkeep, put a spore counter on Elvish Farmer.\\nRemove three spore counters from Elvish Farmer: Create a 1/1 green Saproling creature token.\\nSacrifice a Saproling: You gain 2 life.', 'At the beginning of your upkeep, put a spore counter on Feral Thallid.\\nRemove three spore counters from Feral Thallid: Regenerate Feral Thallid.', 'At the beginning of your upkeep, put a spore counter on Spore Flower.\\nRemove three spore counters from Spore Flower: Prevent all combat damage that would be dealt this turn.', 'At the beginning of your upkeep, put a spore counter on Thallid Devourer.\\nRemove three spore counters from Thallid Devourer: Create a 1/1 green Saproling creature token.\\nSacrifice a Saproling: Thallid Devourer gets +1/+2 until end of turn.', 'At the beginning of your upkeep, put a spore counter on Thallid.\\nRemove three spore counters from Thallid: Create a 1/1 green Saproling creature token.', 'At the beginning of your upkeep, put a time counter on Time Bomb.\\n{1}, {T}, Sacrifice Time Bomb: Time Bomb deals damage equal to the number of time counters on it to each creature and each player.', "At the beginning of your upkeep, sacrifice Earthlink unless you pay {2}.\\nWhenever a creature dies, that creature's controller sacrifices a land.", "At the beginning of your upkeep, sacrifice Nature's Wrath unless you pay {G}.\\nWhenever a player puts an Island or blue permanent onto the battlefield, that player sacrifices an Island or blue permanent.\\nWhenever a player puts a Swamp or black permanent onto the battlefield, that player sacrifices a Swamp or black permanent.", 'At the beginning of your upkeep, you may have Shyft become the color or colors of your choice. (This effect lasts indefinitely.)', 'Attacking creatures get +1/+0 and gain trample until end of turn.', "Aysen Crusader's power and toughness are each equal to 2 plus the number of Soldiers and Warriors you control.", 'Balduvian Hydra enters the battlefield with X +1/+0 counters on it.\\nRemove a +1/+0 counter from Balduvian Hydra: Prevent the next 1 damage that would be dealt to Balduvian Hydra this turn.\\n{R}{R}{R}: Put a +1/+0 counter on Balduvian Hydra. Activate only during your upkeep.', "Banding (Any creatures with banding, and up to one without, can attack in a band. Bands are blocked as a group. If any creatures with banding you control are blocking or being blocked by a creature, you divide that creature's combat damage, not its controller, among any of the creatures it's being blocked by or is blocking.)", "Brassclaw Orcs can't block creatures with power 2 or greater.", "Cast this spell only during combat before blockers are declared.\\nTarget creature can't block this turn.\\nDraw a card at the beginning of the next turn's upkeep.", 'Choose a card name. Exile the top six cards of your library, then reveal cards from the top of your library until you reveal a card with the chosen name. Put that card into your hand and exile all other cards revealed this way.', 'Choose two target creatures an opponent controls. That player chooses and sacrifices one of those creatures. Put a -1/-1 counter on the other.', "Clockwork Steed enters the battlefield with four +1/+0 counters on it.\\nClockwork Steed can't be blocked by artifact creatures.\\nAt end of combat, if Clockwork Steed attacked or blocked this combat, remove a +1/+0 counter from it.\\n{X}, {T}: Put up to X +1/+0 counters on Clockwork Steed. This ability can't cause the total number of +1/+0 counters on Clockwork Steed to be greater than four. Activate only during your upkeep.", "Counter target instant spell if it's blue.\\nDraw a card at the beginning of the next turn's upkeep.", 'Counter target spell.', "Create a 1/1 white Knight creature token with banding. (Any creatures with banding, and up to one without, can attack in a band. Bands are blocked as a group. If any creatures with banding you control are blocking or being blocked by a creature, you divide that creature's combat damage, not its controller, among any of the creatures it's being blocked by or is blocking.)", "Creature spells can't be cast.\\nPay 4 life: Destroy Aether Storm. It can't be regenerated. Any player may activate this ability.", "Creatures without flying don't untap during their controllers' untap steps.\\nAt the beginning of each player's upkeep, that player may choose any number of tapped creatures without flying they control and pay {2} for each creature chosen this way. If the player does, untap those creatures.", 'Cumulative upkeep {1} (At the beginning of your upkeep, put an age counter on this permanent, then sacrifice it unless you pay its upkeep cost for each age counter on it.)\\nAll creatures get -1/-0.\\n{1}{G}: All creatures get -1/-0 until end of turn.', "Cumulative upkeep {1} (At the beginning of your upkeep, put an age counter on this permanent, then sacrifice it unless you pay its upkeep cost for each age counter on it.)\\nPrevent all damage that would be dealt by instant and sorcery spells.\\nCreatures with flying don't untap during their controllers' untap steps.", 'Cumulative upkeep {1} (At the beginning of your upkeep, put an age counter on this permanent, then sacrifice it unless you pay its upkeep cost for each age counter on it.)\\n{1}: Soldevi Simulacrum gets +1/+0 until end of turn.', 'Cumulative upkeep {1} (At the beginning of your upkeep, put an age counter on this permanent, then sacrifice it unless you pay its upkeep cost for each age counter on it.)\\n{T}: Put a music counter on target creature. If it doesn\'t have "At the beginning of your upkeep, destroy this creature unless you pay {1} for each music counter on it," it gains that ability.', 'Cumulative upkeep {1} (At the beginning of your upkeep, put an age counter on this permanent, then sacrifice it unless you pay its upkeep cost for each age counter on it.)\\n{U}, Discard a card: Draw a card.', 'Cumulative upkeep {1}{W} (At the beginning of your upkeep, put an age counter on this permanent, then sacrifice it unless you pay its upkeep cost for each age counter on it.)\\nDamage that would reduce your life total to less than 1 reduces it to 1 instead.', 'Cumulative upkeep {2} (At the beginning of your upkeep, put an age counter on this permanent, then sacrifice it unless you pay its upkeep cost for each age counter on it.)\\nIf a land is tapped for mana, it produces colorless mana instead of any other type.', "Cumulative upkeep {W} (At the beginning of your upkeep, put an age counter on this permanent, then sacrifice it unless you pay its upkeep cost for each age counter on it.)\\nWhenever a Swamp, Mountain, black permanent, or red permanent becomes tapped, Royal Decree deals 1 damage to that permanent's controller.", "Cumulative upkeep—Exile the top card of your library. (At the beginning of your upkeep, put an age counter on this permanent, then sacrifice it unless you pay its upkeep cost for each age counter on it.)\\nWhen a player doesn't pay Thought Lash's cumulative upkeep, that player exiles all cards from their library.\\nExile the top card of your library: Prevent the next 1 damage that would be dealt to you this turn.", "Cumulative upkeep—Pay 1 life. (At the beginning of your upkeep, put an age counter on this permanent, then sacrifice it unless you pay its upkeep cost for each age counter on it.)\\nAt the beginning of each player's upkeep, that player sacrifices a green or white permanent.", "Cumulative upkeep—Pay 2 life. (At the beginning of your upkeep, put an age counter on this permanent, then sacrifice it unless you pay its upkeep cost for each age counter on it.)\\nWhen Glacial Chasm enters the battlefield, sacrifice a land.\\nCreatures you control can't attack.\\nPrevent all damage that would be dealt to you.", 'Cumulative upkeep—Pay {B} and 1 life. (At the beginning of your upkeep, put an age counter on this permanent, then sacrifice it unless you pay its upkeep cost for each age counter on it.)\\nIf a land is tapped for mana, it produces {B} instead of any other type.', 'Death Spark deals 1 damage to any target.\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, if Death Spark is in your graveyard with a creature card directly above it, you may pay {1}. If you do, return Death Spark to your hand.', "Defender (This creature can't attack.)\\nDrift of the Dead's power and toughness are each equal to the number of snow lands you control.", "Defender (This creature can't attack.)\\nFlying\\n{U}: Thunder Wall gets +1/+1 until end of turn.", "Defender (This creature can't attack.)\\nSacrifice Tinder Wall: Add {R}{R}.\\n{R}, Sacrifice Tinder Wall: It deals 2 damage to target creature it's blocking.", "Defender (This creature can't attack.)\\n{1}: Snow Fortress gets +1/+0 until end of turn.\\n{1}: Snow Fortress gets +0/+1 until end of turn.\\n{3}: Snow Fortress deals 1 damage to target creature without flying that's attacking you.", "Defender (This creature can't attack.)\\n{U}{U}, {T}: Create a 0/1 blue Plant Wall creature token with defender named Kelp.", 'Destroy all enchantments or all nonwhite enchantments.', 'Destroy all lands.', 'Destroy all tapped creatures. You gain 2 life for each creature destroyed this way.', 'Destroy all white permanents.', 'Destroy target artifact or enchantment.', "Destroy target artifact or land. It can't be regenerated.", "Destroy target creature with power 4 or greater. It can't be regenerated.", "Destroy target land. If that land was a snow land, Icequake deals 1 damage to that land's controller.", 'Destroy target land. If that land was a snow land, you gain 1 life.', "Destroy target nonartifact attacking creature. It can't be regenerated. Create a black Spirit creature token. Its power is equal to that creature's power and its toughness is equal to that creature's toughness. Sacrifice the token at the beginning of the next end step.", "Destroy target nonblack creature. It can't be regenerated.", 'Draw three cards, then put two cards from your hand on top of your library in any order.', 'Dry Spell deals 1 damage to each creature and each player.', 'Dwarven Ruins enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add {R}.\\n{T}, Sacrifice Dwarven Ruins: Add {R}{R}.', 'Ebon Stronghold enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add {B}.\\n{T}, Sacrifice Ebon Stronghold: Add {B}{B}.', 'Enchant creature card in a graveyard\\nWhen Dance of the Dead enters the battlefield, if it\'s on the battlefield, it loses "enchant creature card in a graveyard" and gains "enchant creature put onto the battlefield with Dance of the Dead." Put enchanted creature card onto the battlefield tapped under your control and attach Dance of the Dead to it. When Dance of the Dead leaves the battlefield, that creature\'s controller sacrifices it.\\nEnchanted creature gets +1/+1 and doesn\'t untap during its controller\'s untap step.\\nAt the beginning of the upkeep of enchanted creature\'s controller, that player may pay {1}{B}. If the player does, untap that creature.', "Enchant creature you control\\nWhenever enchanted creature attacks and isn't blocked, you may have it assign no combat damage this turn. If you do, defending player discards a card at random.", 'Enchant creature\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, sacrifice Binding Grasp unless you pay {1}{U}.\\nYou control enchanted creature.\\nEnchanted creature gets +0/+1.', 'Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature gets +0/+2.\\nSacrifice Carapace: Regenerate enchanted creature.', 'Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature gets +0/+2.\\n{R}: Enchanted creature gets +1/+0 until end of turn.', 'Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature gets +1/+0 and has flying and first strike.', "Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature gets +1/+1.\\n{1}{U}: Return Viscerid Armor to its owner's hand.", 'Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature gets +1/+1.\\n{W}: Enchanted creature gets +0/+1 until end of turn.', "Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature gets +2/+0.\\nAt the beginning of the upkeep of enchanted creature's controller, put a -0/-1 counter on that creature.", 'Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature gets +3/+0 and can only attack alone.', "Enchant creature\\nWhen Krovikan Fetish enters the battlefield, draw a card at the beginning of the next turn's upkeep.\\nEnchanted creature gets +1/+1.", 'Enchant creature\\nWhen enchanted creature leaves the battlefield, its controller sacrifices a creature.', "Enchant creature\\nWhenever enchanted creature attacks and isn't blocked, its controller may have it deal damage equal to its power plus 2 to another target creature. If that player does, the attacking creature assigns no combat damage this turn.", 'Enchant creature\\n{B}, Pay 1 life: Enchanted creature gets +2/+2 until end of turn. Activate no more than three times each turn.', 'Enchant land you control\\nEnchanted land has "{W}{W}, {T}: Create a 0/1 white Caribou creature token."\\nSacrifice a Caribou token: You gain 1 life.', 'Enchant land\\nEnchanted land has "{T}: Target creature gets +2/+1 until end of turn."', 'Enchant land\\nYou control enchanted land.', 'Exile Elvish Spirit Guide from your hand: Add {G}.', 'Exile target creature. Its controller gains life equal to its power.', 'First strike, haste', 'First strike, protection from red', 'First strike, trample\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, put a -2/-2 counter on Ebon Praetor.\\nSacrifice a creature: Remove a -2/-2 counter from Ebon Praetor. If the sacrificed creature was a Thrull, put a +1/+0 counter on Ebon Praetor. Activate only during your upkeep and only once each turn.', "First strike\\n{1}{B}: Regenerate Lim-Dûl's High Guard.", 'Flying, haste', 'Flying, protection from red', 'Flying, vigilance', "Flying; first strike; banding (Any creatures with banding, and up to one without, can attack in a band. Bands are blocked as a group. If any creatures with banding you control are blocking or being blocked by a creature, you divide that creature's combat damage, not its controller, among any of the creatures it's being blocked by or is blocking.)", "Flying\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, put a wage counter on Rogue Skycaptain. You may pay {2} for each wage counter on it. If you don't, remove all wage counters from Rogue Skycaptain and an opponent gains control of it.", "Flying\\nMenace (This creature can't be blocked except by two or more creatures.)", "Flying\\nWhen Angel of Fury dies, you may shuffle it into its owner's library.", 'Flying\\nWhen Fire Dragon enters the battlefield, it deals damage to target creature equal to the number of Mountains you control.', "Flying\\nWhen Ivory Gargoyle dies, return it to the battlefield under its owner's control at the beginning of the next end step and you skip your next draw step.\\n{4}{W}: Exile Ivory Gargoyle.", 'Flying\\nWhen Screeching Drake enters the battlefield, draw a card, then discard a card.', "Flying\\nWhen Sea Drake enters the battlefield, return two target lands you control to their owner's hand.", 'Flying\\nWhenever Sibilant Spirit attacks, defending player may draw a card.', 'Flying\\n{2}: Roterothopter gets +1/+0 until end of turn. Activate no more than twice each turn.', 'Flying\\n{T}: Storm Spirit deals 2 damage to target creature.', 'Flying\\n{T}: Target creature you control with toughness 2 or less gets +1/+1 and gains flying until end of turn. When Phantasmal Mount leaves the battlefield this turn, sacrifice that creature. When the creature leaves the battlefield this turn, sacrifice Phantasmal Mount.', 'Flying\\n{U}, Exile the top card of your library: Tap target creature with flying.\\n{U}, Exile the top card of your library: If the exiled card is a snow land, Storm Elemental gets +1/+1 until end of turn.', "Foul Familiar can't block.\\n{B}, Pay 1 life: Return Foul Familiar to its owner's hand.", 'Green creatures you control get +1/+1.', 'Haste\\n{B}: Return Ashen Ghoul from your graveyard to the battlefield. Activate only during your upkeep and only if three or more creature cards are above Ashen Ghoul.', 'Havenwood Battleground enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add {G}.\\n{T}, Sacrifice Havenwood Battleground: Add {G}{G}.', 'Icatian Javelineers enters the battlefield with a javelin counter on it.\\n{T}, Remove a javelin counter from Icatian Javelineers: It deals 1 damage to any target.', 'Iceberg enters the battlefield with X ice counters on it.\\n{3}: Put an ice counter on Iceberg.\\nRemove an ice counter from Iceberg: Add {C}.', "If Balduvian Trading Post would enter the battlefield, sacrifice an untapped Mountain instead. If you do, put Balduvian Trading Post onto the battlefield. If you don't, put it into its owner's graveyard.\\n{T}: Add {C}{R}.\\n{1}, {T}: Balduvian Trading Post deals 1 damage to target attacking creature.", "If Heart of Yavimaya would enter the battlefield, sacrifice a Forest instead. If you do, put Heart of Yavimaya onto the battlefield. If you don't, put it into its owner's graveyard.\\n{T}: Add {G}.\\n{T}: Target creature gets +1/+1 until end of turn.", "If Kjeldoran Outpost would enter the battlefield, sacrifice a Plains instead. If you do, put Kjeldoran Outpost onto the battlefield. If you don't, put it into its owner's graveyard.\\n{T}: Add {W}.\\n{1}{W}, {T}: Create a 1/1 white Soldier creature token.", "If Soldevi Excavations would enter the battlefield, sacrifice an untapped Island instead. If you do, put Soldevi Excavations onto the battlefield. If you don't, put it into its owner's graveyard.\\n{T}: Add {C}{U}.\\n{1}, {T}: Scry 1.", "Incinerate deals 3 damage to any target. A creature dealt damage this way can't be regenerated this turn.", "Ironclaw Orcs can't block creatures with power 2 or greater.", "Jester's Mask enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{1}, {T}, Sacrifice Jester's Mask: Target opponent puts the cards from their hand on top of their library. Search that player's library for that many cards. That player puts those cards into their hand, then shuffles.", "Lava Burst deals X damage to any target. If Lava Burst would deal damage to a creature, that damage can't be prevented or dealt instead to another permanent or player.", 'Look at the top five cards of your library. Put one of them into your hand and the rest on top of your library in any order.', "Look at the top three cards of target player's library, then put them back in any order. You may have that player shuffle.\\nDraw a card at the beginning of the next turn's upkeep.", "Marjhan doesn't untap during your untap step.\\n{U}{U}, Sacrifice a creature: Untap Marjhan. Activate only during your upkeep.\\nMarjhan can't attack unless defending player controls an Island.\\n{U}{U}: Marjhan gets -1/-0 until end of turn and deals 1 damage to target attacking creature without flying.\\nWhen you control no Islands, sacrifice Marjhan.", 'Meteor Shower deals X plus 1 damage divided as you choose among any number of targets.', "Orcish Conscripts can't attack unless at least two other creatures attack.\\nOrcish Conscripts can't block unless at least two other creatures block.", "Orcish Veteran can't block white creatures with power 2 or greater.\\n{R}: Orcish Veteran gains first strike until end of turn.", 'Prevent all combat damage that would be dealt by target attacking creature this turn.', 'Prevent the next 3 damage that would be dealt to target creature this turn. At the beginning of the next end step, put a +0/+1 counter on that creature for each 1 damage prevented this way.', 'Protection from black\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, Minion of Leshrac deals 5 damage to you unless you sacrifice a creature other than Minion of Leshrac. If Minion of Leshrac deals damage to you this way, tap it.\\n{T}: Destroy target creature or land.', 'Protection from black\\n{W}: Order of the White Shield gains first strike until end of turn.\\n{W}{W}: Order of the White Shield gets +1/+0 until end of turn.', 'Protection from white', 'Protection from white\\n{B}: Knight of Stromgald gains first strike until end of turn.\\n{B}{B}: Knight of Stromgald gets +1/+0 until end of turn.', "Put up to three target cards from an opponent's graveyard on top of their library in any order.", 'Put up to three target creature cards from your graveyard on top of your library.', 'Reach (This creature can block creatures with flying.)\\nWhenever Woolly Spider blocks a creature with flying, Woolly Spider gets +0/+2 until end of turn.', "Red Cliffs Armada can't attack unless defending player controls an Island.", 'Ruins of Trokair enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add {W}.\\n{T}, Sacrifice Ruins of Trokair: Add {W}{W}.', 'Sacrifice a snow Mountain: Prevent all combat damage that would be dealt this turn.', 'Search your library for a card, then shuffle and put that card on top. You lose 2 life.', 'Search your library for a sorcery card, reveal it, then shuffle and put that card on top.', "Shuffle a card from your hand into your library. If you do, draw two cards at the beginning of the next turn's upkeep.", 'Skip your draw step.\\nWhenever you discard a card, exile that card from your graveyard.\\nPay 1 life: Exile the top card of your library face down. Put that card into your hand at the beginning of your next end step.', "Stone Spirit can't be blocked by creatures with flying.", 'Svyelunite Temple enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add {U}.\\n{T}, Sacrifice Svyelunite Temple: Add {U}{U}.', 'Take an extra turn after this one.', "Tap all blocking creatures. Prevent all combat damage that would be dealt this turn. Each attacking creature and each blocking creature doesn't untap during its controller's next untap step.", 'Tap an untapped snow land you control: Karplusan Giant gets +1/+1 until end of turn.', "Tap target artifact, creature, or land.\\nDraw a card at the beginning of the next turn's upkeep.", 'Target creature gets +3/+3 until end of turn.', 'Target creature gets -5/-0 until end of turn.', "Target opponent chooses a card in your graveyard. You may pay {G}. If you do, repeat this process except that opponent can't choose a card already chosen for Forgotten Lore. Then put the last chosen card into your hand.", 'Target player chooses three cards from their hand and puts them on top of their library in any order.', "Trample\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, sacrifice Deep Spawn unless you mill two cards.\\n{U}: Deep Spawn gains shroud until end of turn and doesn't untap during your next untap step. Tap Deep Spawn. (A creature with shroud can't be the target of spells or abilities.)", 'Trample\\nWhenever Aurochs attacks, it gets +1/+0 until end of turn for each other attacking Aurochs.', 'Untap target creature an opponent controls and gain control of it until end of turn. That creature gains haste until end of turn. When you lose control of the creature, tap it.', "When Icy Prison enters the battlefield, exile target creature.\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, sacrifice Icy Prison unless any player pays {3}.\\nWhen Icy Prison leaves the battlefield, return the exiled card to the battlefield under its owner's control.", 'When Imperial Recruiter enters the battlefield, search your library for a creature card with power 2 or less, reveal it, put it into your hand, then shuffle.', 'When Kjeldoran Dead enters the battlefield, sacrifice a creature.\\n{B}: Regenerate Kjeldoran Dead.', "When Phyrexian Devourer's power is 7 or greater, sacrifice it.\\nExile the top card of your library: Put X +1/+1 counters on Phyrexian Devourer, where X is the exiled card's mana value.", 'When you control no Islands, sacrifice Skeleton Ship.\\n{T}: Put a -1/-1 counter on target creature.', "Whenever Farrel's Zealot attacks and isn't blocked, you may have it deal 3 damage to target creature. If you do, Farrel's Zealot assigns no combat damage this turn.", 'Whenever Johtull Wurm becomes blocked, it gets -2/-1 until end of turn for each creature blocking it beyond the first.', "Whenever Joven's Ferrets attacks, it gets +0/+2 until end of turn.\\nAt end of combat, tap all creatures that blocked Joven's Ferrets this turn. They don't untap during their controller's next untap step.", "Whenever Necrite attacks and isn't blocked, you may sacrifice it. If you do, destroy target creature defending player controls. It can't be regenerated.", "Whenever Orcish Squatters attacks and isn't blocked, you may gain control of target land defending player controls for as long as you control Orcish Squatters. If you do, Orcish Squatters assigns no combat damage this turn.", 'Whenever Royal Trooper blocks, it gets +2/+2 until end of turn.', 'Whenever a creature dies, you may pay {3}. If you do, draw a card.', "Whenever a player taps a snow land for mana, that player adds one mana of any type that land produced. That land doesn't untap during its controller's next untap step.", 'Wiitigo enters the battlefield with six +1/+1 counters on it.\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, put a +1/+1 counter on Wiitigo if it has blocked or been blocked since your last upkeep. Otherwise, remove a +1/+1 counter from it.', 'Woolly Mammoths has trample as long as you control a snow land.', "You may choose not to untap Ice Floe during your untap step.\\n{T}: Tap target creature without flying that's attacking you. It doesn't untap during its controller's untap step for as long as Ice Floe remains tapped.", "You may exile a green card from your hand rather than pay this spell's mana cost.\\nDistribute three +1/+1 counters among one, two, or three target creatures. For each +1/+1 counter you put on a creature this way, remove a +1/+1 counter from that creature at the beginning of the next cleanup step.", "You may exile a red card from your hand rather than pay this spell's mana cost.\\nPyrokinesis deals 4 damage divided as you choose among any number of target creatures.", "You may exile a white card from your hand rather than pay this spell's mana cost.\\nPrevent the next 7 damage that would be dealt to any target this turn. If it's a creature, put a +0/+1 counter on it for each 1 damage prevented this way at the beginning of the next end step.", "You may have Wolf Pack assign its combat damage as though it weren't blocked.", "{0}: Varchild's Crusader can't be blocked this turn except by Walls. Sacrifice Varchild's Crusader at the beginning of the next end step.", '{1}, Exile two creature cards from a single graveyard: Create a 1/1 green Saproling creature token.', '{1}, {T}, Sacrifice Aeolipile: It deals 2 damage to any target.', "{1}, {T}, Sacrifice Barbed Sextant: Add one mana of any color. Draw a card at the beginning of the next turn's upkeep.", '{1}, {T}, Sacrifice Elven Lyre: Target creature gets +2/+2 until end of turn.', "{1}, {T}, Sacrifice Lodestone Bauble: Put up to four target basic land cards from a player's graveyard on top of their library in any order. That player draws a card at the beginning of the next turn's upkeep.", '{1}, {T}, Sacrifice a creature: Skull Catapult deals 2 damage to any target.', "{1}, {T}: Put a charge counter on Jeweled Amulet. Note the type of mana spent to pay this activation cost. Activate only if there are no charge counters on Jeweled Amulet.\\n{T}, Remove a charge counter from Jeweled Amulet: Add one mana of Jeweled Amulet's last noted type.", '{1}, {T}: Target creature gains first strike until end of turn.', '{1}: Adarkar Sentinel gets +0/+1 until end of turn.', '{1}: Flip a coin. If you win the flip, target Orc creature gets +2/+0 until end of turn. If you lose the flip, it gets -0/-2 until end of turn.', '{1}{B}, {T}: Target creature gets -1/-1 until end of turn.', "{1}{G}, {T}, Sacrifice a creature: Forests you control become 2/3 creatures until end of turn. They're still lands.", "{1}{G}, {T}: Target creature doesn't untap during its controller's next untap step.", '{1}{G}: Folk of the Pines gets +1/+0 until end of turn.', '{1}{G}: Leaping Lizard gets -0/-1 and gains flying until end of turn.', '{1}{R}: Goblin Ski Patrol gets +2/+0 and gains flying. Its controller sacrifices it at the beginning of the next end step. Activate only once and only if you control a snow Mountain.', "{1}{R}{G}, {T}: Exile Giant Trap Door Spider and target creature without flying that's attacking you.", '{1}{U}, {T}: Untap target artifact an opponent controls and gain control of it until end of turn. It gains haste until end of turn. When you lose control of the artifact, tap it.', '{1}{U}: Return target white or black creature card from your graveyard to the battlefield. That creature gains "Cumulative upkeep {2}." If the creature would leave the battlefield, exile it instead of putting it anywhere else. (At the beginning of its controller\'s upkeep, that player puts an age counter on it, then sacrifices it unless they pay its upkeep cost for each age counter on it.)', '{1}{W}: Prevent the next 1 damage that would be dealt to any target this turn.', '{2}, Exile the top two cards of your library: Whirling Catapult deals 1 damage to each creature with flying and each player.', '{2}: Put the top card of your graveyard on the bottom of your library.', '{2}{R}, Exile a creature card from your graveyard: Create a 3/1 black and red Graveborn creature token with haste. Sacrifice it at the beginning of the next end step.', '{2}{U}{U}: Look at the top five cards of your library, put one of them into your hand, and exile the rest.', '{3}, {T}: Exile the top card of your library. Until the beginning of your next upkeep, you may play that card.', '{3}, {T}: Target player looks at the top three cards of their library, puts one of them back on top of their library, then exiles the rest.', '{3}: If your library has ten or more cards in it, target opponent looks at the top ten cards of your library and separates them into two face-down piles. Exile one of those piles. Search the other pile for a card, put it into your hand, then shuffle the rest of that pile into your library.', "{3}: Look at the top three cards of target player's library, then put them back in any order.", "{B}: Phantasmal Fiend gets +1/-1 until end of turn.\\n{1}{U}: Switch Phantasmal Fiend's power and toughness until end of turn.", '{G}: Yavimaya Ancients gets +1/-2 until end of turn.', '{G}{G}: Put a spore counter on target Fungus.', "{G}{W}, Discard a card: Put a +1/+1 counter on target creature or that creature gains banding, first strike, or trample. (This effect lasts indefinitely. Any creatures with banding, and up to one without, can attack in a band. Bands are blocked as a group. If any creatures with banding a player controls are blocking or being blocked by a creature, that player divides that creature's combat damage, not its controller, among any of the creatures it's being blocked by or is blocking.)", '{R}: Flame Spirit gets +1/+0 until end of turn.', '{T}, Discard a nonblack card: Draw a card.\\n{T}, Discard a black card: Draw two cards, then discard one of them.', '{T}, Pay 1 life: Counter target black spell.', '{T}, Pay 1 life: Counter target white spell.', '{T}, Sacrifice Armor Thrull: Put a +1/+2 counter on target creature.', '{T}, Sacrifice Gangrenous Zombies: Gangrenous Zombies deals 1 damage to each creature and each player. If you control a snow Swamp, Gangrenous Zombies deals 2 damage to each creature and each player instead.', "{T}, Sacrifice Mishra's Groundbreaker: Target land becomes a 3/3 artifact creature that's still a land. (This effect lasts indefinitely.)", '{T}, Sacrifice a Forest: Add three mana in any combination of {R} and/or {G}.', "{T}, Sacrifice a creature and a Swamp: Destroy target nonartifact creature. It can't be regenerated.\\n{T}, Sacrifice a creature and a snow Swamp: Destroy target creature. It can't be regenerated.", '{T}, Sacrifice a creature: Target creature gets +2/+2 until end of turn.\\n{1}{U}{U}, Sacrifice a creature: Counter target creature spell.', '{T}, Sacrifice another Orc or Goblin: Other Orc creatures get +1/+1 until end of turn.', "{T}: Destroy target permanent you own. It can't be regenerated.", "{T}: Exile a card from your hand face down. You may look at it for as long as it remains exiled.\\n{T}: Return a card you own exiled with Gustha's Scepter to your hand.\\nWhen you lose control of Gustha's Scepter, put all cards exiled with Gustha's Scepter into their owner's graveyard.", '{T}: Orcish Cannoneers deals 2 damage to any target and 3 damage to you.', '{T}: Tap target creature with power 2 or less.', '{T}: Target creature gets +2/+2 until end of turn. When that creature leaves the battlefield this turn, sacrifice Kjeldoran Elite Guard. Activate only during combat.', "{T}: Target land becomes a Swamp until its controller's next untap step.", "{T}: Target snow land becomes a 2/2 creature until end of turn. It's still a land.", '{T}: Zuran Spellcaster deals 1 damage to any target.', '{U}: Sea Spirit gets +1/+0 until end of turn.', "{X}, {T}: Target opponent mills a card, then repeats this process until a creature card or X cards have been put into their graveyard this way, whichever comes first. If one or more creature cards were put into that graveyard this way, sacrifice Helm of Obedience and put one of them onto the battlefield under your control. X can't be 0.", '{X}{X}{1}: Destroy target noncreature artifact with mana value X.']
flavor: ['"A mage must be precise as well as potent; cautious, as well as clever."\\n—Zur the Enchanter', '"A renegade rallying the rabble does not a true crusader make."\\n—Irini Sengir', '"A whole skin is worth a thousand victories."\\n—Orcish veteran of the Battle of Montford', '"AIIIEEEE!"\\n—Ib Halfheart, goblin tactician', '"All the knowledge of Lat-Nam could not protect its sages from the Brothers\' War."\\n—Gerda Äagesdotter, Archmage of the Unseen', '"Although fragile, the aeolipile could be quite destructive."\\n—*Sarpadian Empires, vol. I*', '"Anybody want some . . . toast?"\\n—Jaya Ballard, task mage', '"As the climate cooled, many elves turned to thallid farming for food, while the hunters honed their skills on what little game remained."\\n—*Sarpadian Empires, vol. III*', '"Be open to the blessings, whatever their form."\\n—Kaysa, elder druid of the Juniper Order', '"Because the orc hordes attacked along the entire border, Scouts were essential to Icatia\'s defense."\\n—*Sarpadian Empires, vol. VI*', '"Born and bred of fungus, thallids were nearly impossible to kill."\\n—*Sarpadian Empires, vol. I*', '"Capturing this specimen was not easy. Study it well, that you someday might be as versatile."\\n—Gerda Äagesdotter, Archmage of the Unseen', '"Come to us, with your lightning. Come to us, with your thunder. Serve us with your strength, and smite our foes with your power."\\n—Steinar Icefist, Balduvian shaman', '"Direct confrontation never was to the orcs\' taste."\\n—General Varchild', '"Divine gifts are granted to those who are worthy."\\n—Halvor Arenson, Kjeldoran priest', '"Do not fear adversity. Let your courage be your strength."\\n—Onatah, Anaba shaman', '"Each generation teaches the next that artifice is the enemy of natural order."\\n—Kaysa, elder druid of the Juniper Order', '"Eenie, meenie, minie, moe . . . oh, why not all of them?"\\n—Jaya Ballard, task mage', '"Every patch of land must belong to Kjeldor, no matter what the cost!"\\n—General Varchild', '"Fair fight? I\'ll take survival over chivalry any day!"\\n—Tor Wauki, Bandit King', '"Faith is our greatest protector."\\n—Halvor Arensson, Kjeldoran priest', '"Finally we understand the lesson of our home: loss begets renewal."\\n—Kolbjörn, elder druid of the Juniper Order', '"For those of courage, even the sky holds no limit."\\n—Arnjlot Olasson, sky mage', '"Fortune does not side with the fainthearted."\\n—Sophocles, Phaedra', '"Freyalise has cleansed our bodies and minds of the plagues of Kjeldor; all she asks in return is that we keep pure our newly given home in Fyndhorn."\\n—Kolbjörn, elder druid of the Juniper Order', '"GOTCHA!"\\n—Jaya Ballard, task mage', '"Here in Fyndhorn, the goddess Freyalise is generous to her children."\\n—Kolbjörn, elder druid of the Juniper Order', '"How can any human hope to match our skills? We are children of Fyndhorn, and its sap runs in our veins."\\n—Taaveti of Kelsinko, elvish hunter', '"How did I ever let myself get talked into this project?"\\n—Toothlicker Harj, orcish captain', '"I breathed deeply, and suddenly I knew not who or where I was."\\n—Taaveti of Kelsinko, elvish hunter', '"I do love the rain . . . but this storm feels somehow wrong, Taysir."\\n—Daria', '"I have seen the true path. I will not warm myself by the fire—I will become the flame."\\n—Lim-Dûl, the Necromancer', '"I implore you not to forget the horrors of the past. You would have us start the Brothers\' War anew!"\\n—Sorine Relicbane, Soldevi heretic', '"I never question the Autumn Willow about her motives, not even when she turns people into lizards. It\'s her way."\\n—Devin, faerie noble', '"I reeled from the blow, and then suddenly, I knew exactly what to do. Within moments, victory was mine."\\n—Gustha Ebbasdotter, Kjeldoran royal mage', '"I thought the day had brought enough horrors for our ragged band, but the night was far worse."\\n—Lucilde Fiksdotter, leader of the Order of the White Shield', '"I would say that our bureaucrats are no better than vipers—but I shouldn\'t insult the vipers."\\n—Murat, death speaker', '"If Heaven has placed it in your hands, it means that the throne is destined to be yours."', '"If we do our duty and uphold our honor, Kjeldor shall stand for a thousand years."\\n—Arna Kennerüd, skyknight', '"If you\'d been there, you would\'ve run from that deer, too!"\\n—Jaya Ballard, Task Mage', '"Ihsan, the weak. Ihsan, the fallen. Ihsan, the betrayer. He has brought shame to the Serra paladins where none existed before. May his suffering equal his betrayal."\\n—Baris, Serra inquisitor', '"In these troubled times, we alone carry the hope of reconciliation between Elf and Human."\\n—Jaeuhl Carthalion, Juniper Order advocate', '"It is the changing of perception that is important."\\n—Gerda Äagesdotter, Archmage of the Unseen', '"It rose above our heads, above the ship, and still higher yet. No foggy, ice-laden sea in the world could frighten me more."\\n—General Jarkeld, the Arctic Fox', '"It\'s a thankless job, and you\'ll probably die in an explosion. But the pay is pretty good."\\n—Toothlicker Harj, orcish captain', '"Keep your chainmail, warrior. I have my own form of protection."\\n—Halvor Arenson, Kjeldoran priest', '"Kjeldor must be supreme at any cost."\\n—Avram Garrisson, leader of the Knights of Stromgald', '"Kjeldorans should rule supreme, and to the rest, death!"\\n—Avram Garrisson, leader of the Knights of Stromgald', '"Let any who doubt the evil of using the ancient devices look at this infernal machine. What manner of fiend would design such a sadistic device?"\\n—Sorine Relicbane, Soldevi heretic', '"Let them send their legions! I will show them that my truth is stronger than their swords."\\n—General Varchild', '"Let us remember brave Jarkeld and his troops, who perished in the Adarkar Wastes so long ago."\\n—Halvor Arenson, Kjeldoran priest', '"Magic overused can freeze the mind. Creativity is more important than power."\\n—Zur the Enchanter', '"Mammoths may be good to ride on, but they\'re certainly bad to fall off of!"\\n—Disa the Restless, journal entry', '"May they speed to their task, for the skyknights alone cannot hold Kjeldor safe."\\n—Arna Kennerüd, skycaptain', '"More than lessons may be gained from the past."\\n—Halvor Arensson, Kjeldoran priest', '"Once great literature—now great litter."\\n—Jaya Ballard, task mage', '"Our friends of the forest take many forms, yet all serve the will of Freyalise."\\n—Laina of the Elvish Council', '"Overkill? This isn\'t a game of Kick-the-Ouphe!"\\n—Jaya Ballard, task mage', '"Rarely have power and madness been so delightfully wed as they have in our dear grandmother."\\n—Baron Sengir', '"Relax. I\'m sure it\'s just a snake hissing."\\n—Avram Garrisson, leader of the Knights of Stromgald', '"Rumors persist of dark deeds performed in the depths of Soldev. When will Dagsson heed the danger therein?"\\n—Sorine Relicbane, Soldevi heretic', '"Serve me, and live forever."\\n—Lim-Dûl, the Necromancer', '"Shall we turn away a worthy soul because his parents were peasants? I think not."\\n—Lucilde Fiksdotter, leader of the Order of the White Shield', '"So large and so quiet—a combination best avoided."\\n—Disa the Restless, journal entry', '"Take their dead, and entomb them in the snow. Risen, they shall serve a new purpose."\\n—Lim-Dûl, the Necromancer', '"Thallids could absorb energy from the forest itself. Even elves were at a disadvantage in fighting them."\\n—*Sarpadian Empires, vol. III*', '"That which does not bend to the will of Freyalise shall surely break."\\n—Kolbjörn, elder druid of the Juniper Order', '"The An-Zerrins have served me well, ever since I first killed them."\\n—Baron Sengir', '"The duel was going badly for me, and Zur thought I was finished. He boasted that he would eat my soul—but all he ate were his words."\\n—Gustha Ebbasdotter, Kjeldoran royal mage', '"The folk of the Karplusan mountains are impossible to ambush."\\n—Lovisa Coldeyes, Balduvian chieftain', '"The guard will forever stand ready. For them, death is merely an inconvenience, not an ending."\\n—Chaeska, Keeper of Tresserhorn', '"The lemures had barely taken wing when the sky roared with thunder. The swarm of little beasts wavered, divided, and fell, crashing to the earth."\\n—General Jarkeld, the Arctic Fox', '"The magic at the heart of all living things can bear awe-inspiring fruit."\\n—Kolevi of Havenwood, elder druid', '"The meek shall fight as one, and they shall overcome even the greatest of foes."\\n—Halvor Arensson, Kjeldoran priest', '"The roterothoper is as insidious as it is ingenious. It is one of the few creations of our school that I take no pride in."\\n—Baki, wizard attendant', '"The sea gives up her dead as easily as the soil."\\n—Lim-Dûl, the Necromancer', '"The shaman waved the staff, and the land itself went mad."\\n—Disa the Restless, journal entry', '"The shamans of Marit Lage do her bidding in secret, but they do it gladly."\\n—Halvor Arenson, Kjeldoran priest', '"The so-called barbarians will not respect us for our military might—they will respect us for our honor."\\n—Lucilde Fiksdotter, leader of the Order of the White Shield', '"The spirit of the flame is the spirit of change."\\n—Lovisa Coldeyes, Balduvian chieftain', '"The spirit of the stone is the spirit of strength."\\n—Lovisa Coldeyes, Balduvian chieftain', '"The very lands of Balduvia are alive."\\n—Arna Kennerüd, skyknight', '"The worst thing about being a mercenary for the Ebon Hand is having to wear a dead thrull."\\n—Ivra Jursdotter', '"There is no shame in solitude. The lone knight may succeed where a hundred founder."\\n—Arna Kennerüd, skyknight', '"These sorcerers always seem to have another surprise up their sleeves."\\n—Zur the Enchanter', '"They aren\'t the brightest or the quickest of giants. For that matter, the same holds true if you compare them to rocks."\\n—Disa the Restless, journal entry', '"They shall kill those whom once they loved."\\n—Lim-Dûl, the Necromancer', '"This ceaseless device has helped uncover marvels unreachable by mere flesh."\\n—Arcum Dagsson, Soldevi machinist', '"This party is such fun—but it\'s a shame to mourn just one."\\n—Irini Sengir', '"Thorn bushes spring up wherever the army has passed. Lean years follow in the wake of a great war."\\n—Lao Tzu, Tao Te Ching, trans. Feng and English', '"Though Serra has not been seen for twenty years, her gargoyles still watch over our city and punish the guilty."\\n—Gulsen, abbey matron', '"To bring her down we must be on all sides at once—leave one avenue open and we\'ll all be dead."\\n—Taaveti of Kelsinko, elvish hunter', '"To visit the sky requires bravery, and thought, and little else. To master the sky requires the binding of its masters, and little else."\\n—Arnjlot Olasson, sky mage', '"Too many of us have died in the explosions that wrack these hills."\\n—Klazina Jansdotter, leader of the Order of the Sacred Torch', '"Trust in the power of stone. Stone is strong; stone shatters swords; stone breaks bones. Trust in stone."\\n—Lovisa Coldeyes, Balduvian chieftain', '"We are never without guidance, if we but seek it."\\n—Taaveti of Kelsinko, elvish hunter', '"We could see the horizon blacken with the great beasts, but it was too late. The icefield offered no immediate safety, but luckily most of us reached a crevasse in which we could take cover."\\n—Disa the Restless, journal entry', '"We encountered the sentinels in the wastes, near no living thing. Their purpose was inscrutable."\\n—Disa the Restless, journal entry', '"We need not fear the forces of the air; I\'ve yet to see a spider without an appetite."\\n—Taaveti of Kelsinko, elvish hunter', '"We orphans of Fyndhorn have found no welcome in this alien place."\\n—Taaveti of Kelsinko, elvish hunter', '"We were chasing Lim-Dûl when the ridge in front of us suddenly crumbled. I can\'t believe it was mere coincidence."\\n—Lucilde Fiksdotter, leader of the Order of the White Shield', '"We were not meant to have such terrible things. They should be left where we found them, if not destroyed!"\\n—Sorine Relicbane, Soldevi heretic', '"Were they to reduce us to ash, we would clog their throats and sting their eyes in payment."\\n—Lovisa Coldeyes, Balduvian chieftain', '"What I want, I take."\\n—Gustha Ebbasdotter, Kjeldoran royal mage', '"When the earth shakes, and their animals are swallowed up by the ground, perhaps they will think twice before attacking again."\\n—Lim-Dûl, the Necromancer', '"When you cannot rely on your sources, trust your own senses. When you cannot trust those, you must follow your instincts."\\n—Lovisa Coldeyes, Balduvian chieftain', '"Wherever water is lacking, all things suffer."\\n—Autumn Willow', '"Who needs a spear? Ya break off the horn, and ya stab the fish with it. Easy!"\\n—Kakra, sea troll', '"Why do we trade with those despicable elves? You don\'t live in forests, you burn them!"\\n—Avram Garrisson, leader of the Knights of Stromgald', '"Will not the mountains quake and hills melt at the coming of the darkness? Share this vision with your enemies, Lim-Dûl, and they shall wither."\\n—Leshrac, Walker of Night', '"Without combat medics, Icatia would probably not have withstood the forces of chaos as long as it did."\\n—*Sarpadian Empires, vol. VI*', '"Worlds turn in crucial moments of decision. Make your choice."\\n—Gustha Ebbasdotter, Kjeldoran royal mage', '"Ya can eat it or ya can weave it, but ya can\'t fight in it."\\n—Zeki, reef pirate', '"Yes, I think \'toast\' is an appropriate description."\\n—Jaya Ballard, task mage', '"Yes, the farmers keep our soldiers fed. But why do they have to make every battlefield a pigpen?"\\n—Toothlicker Harj, orcish captain', '"You have almost completed your four years, my son. Soon you shall be a skyknight."\\n—Arna Kennerüd, skyknight', '"Your army must fear you more than the enemy. Only then will you triumph."\\n—Malga Phlegmtooth', 'A blazing light to drive out the shadows.', "A fallen viscerid's only tribute is to be worn by a comrade.", 'By the battle of Red Cliffs in the year 208, the Wu kingdom controlled more than seven thousand warships on the Yangtze.', "Doing something at the last minute isn't so bad when you can make that minute last.", 'Even after the wall was breached in half a dozen places, the phalanxes fought on, standing solidly against the onrushing raiders. Disciplined and dedicated, they held their ranks to the end, even in the face of tremendous losses.', 'Farrel and his followers became a formidable band of vigilantes, battling Icatians and followers of Tourach.', "Few remember that Ashnod's defilement of Terisiare's resources outstripped even that of her peers.", 'Generations of genetic weeding have given rise to the deviously cowardly Ironclaw clan.', 'In ashes are the gems of history.', 'Kaysa speaks as the elder druid, but Yavimaya recognizes only one voice: its own.', 'Necrites killed Jherana Rure, ending the counterinsurgency.', 'Never underestimate the power of the soul unleashed.', "Not all of Terisiare's flooding was natural . . . .", 'Not wind, but the breath of the dead.', 'One aurochs may feed a village, but a herd will flatten it.', 'Scholars are uncertain whether it was the actual sound or some other magical property of the elven lyre that transformed its player.', 'Some Krovikans find strength in the ears and eyes of their victims and wear such fetishes into battle.', 'The elves gathered huge piles of rot to grow fungus. Out of imitation or forethought, the thallids did the same.', "The very ground yielded to Mishra's wishes.", 'The winged helms of the guard are put on for pageants—but taken off for war.', "There's a chance to win every battle.", 'They look human—until they bleed.', 'Unsuccessful in their early battle for Montford, the orcs quickly tempered their bloodlust with cowardice.']
artist: ['Alan Rabinowitz', 'Allen Williams', 'Amy Weber', 'Amy Weber & Tom Wänerstrand', 'Andi Rusu', 'Anson Maddocks', 'Anthony S. Waters', 'Bradley Williams', 'Brian Snõddy', 'Bryon Wackwitz', 'Charles Gillespie', 'Christopher Rush', 'Cornelius Brudi', 'D. Alexander Gregory', 'Dan Frazier', 'Daniel Gelon', 'David A. Cherry', 'Dennis Detwiller', 'Diana Vick', 'Douglas Shuler', 'Drew Tucker', 'Edward P. Beard, Jr.', 'Fang Yue', 'Harold McNeill', 'Heather Hudson', 'James Allen', 'Jeff A. Menges', 'Jesper Myrfors', 'John Coulthart', 'John Matson', 'Julie Baroh', 'Justin Hampton', 'Kaja Foglio', 'Keith Parkinson', 'Ken Meyer, Jr.', 'Li Tie', 'Liz Danforth', 'Margaret Organ-Kean', 'Mark Poole', 'Mark Tedin', 'Melissa A. Benson', 'Mike Kimble', 'Mike Raabe', 'Mitsuaki Sagiri', 'Nicola Leonard', 'NéNé Thomas', 'NéNé Thomas & Catherine Buck', 'Pat Lewis', 'Pete Venters', 'Phil Foglio', 'Quinton Hoover', 'Randy Asplund-Faith', 'Randy Gallegos', 'Rebecca Guay', 'Richard Kane Ferguson', 'Richard Thomas', 'Rick Emond', 'Rob Alexander', 'Ron Spencer', 'Ruth Thompson', 'Sandra Everingham', 'Scott Kirschner', 'Scott M. Fischer', 'Susan Van Camp', 'Terese Nielsen', 'Todd Lockwood', 'Tom Wänerstrand', 'William Simpson', 'Yang Jun Kwon', 'Zhang Jiazhen']
